WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:05.009
- Hello, Believe Nation,
I'm Evan Carmichael.

00:00:05.009 --> 00:00:07.802
My one word is believe and
I believe that entrepreneurs

00:00:07.802 --> 00:00:10.454
will solve all the major
problems of the world.

00:00:10.454 --> 00:00:11.566
So to help you on your journey,

00:00:11.566 --> 00:00:13.582
today I'm going to talk
about the seven ways

00:00:13.582 --> 00:00:17.299
smart people work less and get more done.

00:00:17.299 --> 00:00:20.117
- [Narrator] Nine, eight.

00:00:20.117 --> 00:00:22.867
(exciting music)

00:00:28.602 --> 00:00:30.524
- Number one is create a schedule.

00:00:30.524 --> 00:00:33.311
Successful people for the
most part have a schedule.

00:00:33.311 --> 00:00:34.210
When you have a schedule

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:35.890
and you know what you're
going to get done that day,

00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:38.548
it's easier to stick with it
and plan your big things out.

00:00:38.548 --> 00:00:41.389
So what's really important,
what I find really helpful

00:00:41.389 --> 00:00:43.784
is once a quarter I do
a big audit of my life

00:00:43.784 --> 00:00:45.806
of my business, where
am I spending my time,

00:00:45.806 --> 00:00:47.357
where am I getting the most value from?

00:00:47.357 --> 00:00:50.259
Do my actions map to the big things

00:00:50.259 --> 00:00:52.193
that I'm trying to create for myself?

00:00:52.193 --> 00:00:54.153
And so if my big goal is I want to get

00:00:54.153 --> 00:00:56.567
a million subscribers on
YouTube as an example,

00:00:56.567 --> 00:00:58.487
that's one of my goals, how do I do that

00:00:58.487 --> 00:01:00.820
and are my actions mapping
to that consistently?

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:03.157
So once a week, I have a YouTube day.

00:01:03.157 --> 00:01:04.306
I'm researching.

00:01:04.306 --> 00:01:05.777
I'm trying to better
understand the algorithm.

00:01:05.777 --> 00:01:07.615
I'm trying to update my
thumbnails and titles,

00:01:07.615 --> 00:01:09.290
trying to research new story ideas,

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:11.279
new potential videos that we can put out

00:01:11.279 --> 00:01:13.809
and so I'm constantly
adjusting my schedule

00:01:13.809 --> 00:01:16.218
to map to achieving those big goals.

00:01:16.218 --> 00:01:17.610
So if you know what you're going to do,

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:20.880
you wake up every day with
a schedule that is on point

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.800
and helping guide you
towards your big picture,

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:26.050
you're much more likely to get it done.

00:01:27.839 --> 00:01:30.737
Number two is batch
similar tasks together.

00:01:30.737 --> 00:01:32.749
This one really saved my life.

00:01:32.749 --> 00:01:35.653
It saved so much time out of my schedule

00:01:35.653 --> 00:01:38.063
where anything that you're
doing multiple times per day,

00:01:38.063 --> 00:01:39.043
do once per day.

00:01:39.043 --> 00:01:40.760
Multiple times per week, do once per week.

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:42.436
Multiple times per
month, do once per month.

00:01:42.436 --> 00:01:43.743
The more you can do that,

00:01:43.743 --> 00:01:46.625
the more success you'll have
at getting more stuff done.

00:01:46.625 --> 00:01:49.120
So as an example for making
these YouTube videos,

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:52.932
I will make most of the
videos once a month.

00:01:52.932 --> 00:01:54.669
So I come in here, it's
a Wednesday afternoon

00:01:54.669 --> 00:01:57.240
when I'm filming and
we'll spend the whole day

00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:58.913
making YouTube videos
and I'll batch them out

00:01:58.913 --> 00:02:00.107
for the entire month.

00:02:00.107 --> 00:02:04.822
We'll film between 16, 18
different videos in one sitting

00:02:04.822 --> 00:02:07.692
all day long because
one, I'm in the mindset,

00:02:07.692 --> 00:02:08.525
I'm in the mode.

00:02:08.525 --> 00:02:10.465
We don't have to worry
about setup, take down.

00:02:10.465 --> 00:02:12.115
Also, me being able to be comfortable

00:02:12.115 --> 00:02:14.574
in front of the camera,
share my story, have energy.

00:02:14.574 --> 00:02:15.801
All of that stuff really works

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:18.297
where if you're switching
between tasks constantly,

00:02:18.297 --> 00:02:19.695
it's easy to fall off.

00:02:19.695 --> 00:02:20.837
If you're in writing mode,

00:02:20.837 --> 00:02:22.633
I remember being in
writing mode for my book

00:02:22.633 --> 00:02:24.593
and I'm writing and researching,
I'm in introvert mode,

00:02:24.593 --> 00:02:26.035
don't want to talk to anybody.

00:02:26.035 --> 00:02:28.406
To then prepare for a
call that's coming up,

00:02:28.406 --> 00:02:30.691
that half hour to an hour before the call,

00:02:30.691 --> 00:02:31.955
I'm not being as productive.

00:02:31.955 --> 00:02:33.388
I'm researching who that person is.

00:02:33.388 --> 00:02:35.722
I'm getting nervous about
the call and what's happening

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:38.863
and so I find it really hard
to switch between tasks.

00:02:38.863 --> 00:02:42.336
If I'm going to do an
introvert, creative writing day,

00:02:42.336 --> 00:02:44.081
I spend the whole day doing that.

00:02:44.081 --> 00:02:45.738
Wednesdays I make my YouTube videos.

00:02:45.738 --> 00:02:47.482
Thursday's my public facing day

00:02:47.482 --> 00:02:51.178
so I'll do interviews and
podcast and radio shows

00:02:51.178 --> 00:02:53.902
and guest appearances on other
people's YouTube channels

00:02:53.902 --> 00:02:55.349
and phone calls and meetings.

00:02:55.349 --> 00:02:58.596
I'm in my extrovert mode
and I'll put my hoodie on

00:02:58.596 --> 00:02:59.888
and I go from one meeting to the next

00:02:59.888 --> 00:03:01.021
to the next to the next to the next

00:03:01.021 --> 00:03:02.611
back to back to back to back to back

00:03:02.611 --> 00:03:05.063
and it really helps me
stay in that same energy

00:03:05.063 --> 00:03:09.521
and get more stuff done and so
batch similar tasks together

00:03:09.521 --> 00:03:12.104
to help you be more productive.

00:03:14.515 --> 00:03:16.108
Number three is bring on a team.

00:03:16.108 --> 00:03:19.091
You cannot do everything on
your own as an entrepreneur.

00:03:19.091 --> 00:03:20.895
At the start, I get it, maybe yes.

00:03:20.895 --> 00:03:21.887
You're trying to do everything

00:03:21.887 --> 00:03:23.762
'cause you don't have the
resources yet to build

00:03:23.762 --> 00:03:25.312
but as soon as you can afford it

00:03:25.312 --> 00:03:26.145
or as soon as you can think

00:03:26.145 --> 00:03:28.827
of how you can bring other
people on board, it's so worth it

00:03:28.827 --> 00:03:32.953
because you have genius
level talent at something

00:03:32.953 --> 00:03:35.363
and yet usually that thing
that you're so great at,

00:03:35.363 --> 00:03:37.571
you're only spending 10% of your time on

00:03:37.571 --> 00:03:40.518
and 90% is spent on all the other stuff

00:03:40.518 --> 00:03:42.034
that's involved in running the business.

00:03:42.034 --> 00:03:44.404
The more you can get rid of those things

00:03:44.404 --> 00:03:46.569
and give them to other
people who love doing it

00:03:46.569 --> 00:03:48.576
even if it's hiring
somebody for one hour a day

00:03:48.576 --> 00:03:51.233
which is what I did with my
first hire in my business,

00:03:51.233 --> 00:03:52.871
it alleviates some of the pressure

00:03:52.871 --> 00:03:55.118
to allow you to focus on
what you are great it.

00:03:55.118 --> 00:03:58.020
If you want to go far,
you have to go with a team

00:03:58.020 --> 00:04:00.508
so start looking at who is around you

00:04:00.508 --> 00:04:01.740
that you can bring on board

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:03.672
to take some of those tasks off your plate

00:04:03.672 --> 00:04:07.839
so you could focus on what you
are genius level talent at.

00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:14.278
- Hey, I'm John Sonmez from
Simple Programmer channel

00:04:14.278 --> 00:04:18.445
and tip number four is know
exactly what you're going to do

00:04:19.334 --> 00:04:20.784
before you sit down

00:04:20.784 --> 00:04:23.263
or you let your fingers
touch the keyboard.

00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:24.244
This is one of those things

00:04:24.244 --> 00:04:28.232
that I have found has really
helped me to be more productive

00:04:28.232 --> 00:04:30.977
because if I just put my
fingers on the keyboard,

00:04:30.977 --> 00:04:33.579
if I just sit down and
type at my computer,

00:04:33.579 --> 00:04:37.674
I'll instantly type in there
facebook.com or gmail.com

00:04:37.674 --> 00:04:39.966
so always before I start anything,

00:04:39.966 --> 00:04:41.725
before I go to the computer,

00:04:41.725 --> 00:04:44.546
before I open up my laptop,
I think to myself and I say,

00:04:44.546 --> 00:04:47.900
what am I trying to accomplish,
what am I trying to do?

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:51.787
And by doing that, it stops
me from wasting a lot of time

00:04:51.787 --> 00:04:54.215
and just the little bit
of five minutes here,

00:04:54.215 --> 00:04:57.557
five minutes there that you
spend browsing the internet

00:04:57.557 --> 00:05:00.096
or doing something or distracting yourself

00:05:00.096 --> 00:05:02.544
can lead to a lot of procrastination

00:05:02.544 --> 00:05:04.224
and can prevent you from
getting things done.

00:05:04.224 --> 00:05:05.905
So quick tip to remember.

00:05:05.905 --> 00:05:09.108
Just remember, before you
sit down to do any work,

00:05:09.108 --> 00:05:12.089
before you do anything,
know exactly what it is

00:05:12.089 --> 00:05:13.526
that you're supposed to do

00:05:13.526 --> 00:05:15.286
and then when you unlock your computer

00:05:15.286 --> 00:05:17.168
or put your fingers on the keyboard

00:05:17.168 --> 00:05:20.080
or you sit down in your chair,
that's what you start doing

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:22.826
and you don't just go to
some social media site.

00:05:22.826 --> 00:05:23.659
Alright.

00:05:27.076 --> 00:05:29.016
- Number five is eliminate.

00:05:29.016 --> 00:05:30.038
So I mentioned at the top

00:05:30.038 --> 00:05:32.453
how I love doing a quarterly
audit of my schedule.

00:05:32.453 --> 00:05:35.328
It's so so so so important
'cause you'll often find things

00:05:35.328 --> 00:05:37.289
that you should not be doing anymore.

00:05:37.289 --> 00:05:39.255
So as an example, I
have a mastermind group

00:05:39.255 --> 00:05:42.206
and I used to keep
minutes of every meeting.

00:05:42.206 --> 00:05:43.880
I thought that was the
professional thing to do.

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:45.026
I thought I was adding a lot of value.

00:05:45.026 --> 00:05:47.338
I keep track of what everybody was doing,

00:05:47.338 --> 00:05:48.885
what they said they were going to do

00:05:48.885 --> 00:05:51.179
and report back and send them the email

00:05:51.179 --> 00:05:53.225
every month after the
meeting and say, hey,

00:05:53.225 --> 00:05:54.900
here's what we talked about,
here are the minute notes.

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:58.987
One month, I got too busy and
I wasn't able to get it out

00:05:58.987 --> 00:06:01.601
and what happened was nothing.

00:06:01.601 --> 00:06:02.704
Nobody cared.

00:06:02.704 --> 00:06:05.122
And so the next month, as a test,

00:06:05.122 --> 00:06:07.625
I didn't send the minutes out again either

00:06:07.625 --> 00:06:09.880
and nobody cared, nobody
emailed me, nobody called me,

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:11.925
nobody wrote to me, nobody
asked where they were.

00:06:11.925 --> 00:06:13.398
So here I was doing this service

00:06:13.398 --> 00:06:14.829
that I thought was really valuable.

00:06:14.829 --> 00:06:17.778
It was a quality value
add for my customers

00:06:17.778 --> 00:06:19.494
and nobody actually cared about it

00:06:19.494 --> 00:06:21.957
and so ever since then, I
stopped doing minute notes.

00:06:21.957 --> 00:06:23.349
There are things that you are doing

00:06:23.349 --> 00:06:25.821
in your day to day calendar,
in your day to day schedule

00:06:25.821 --> 00:06:28.684
that you may think is adding
value but really isn't

00:06:28.684 --> 00:06:30.602
and if you can eliminate those,

00:06:30.602 --> 00:06:32.601
take that chunk of time
out of your schedule

00:06:32.601 --> 00:06:36.268
then you can focus on
higher priority tasks.

00:06:38.257 --> 00:06:39.691
Number six is automate.

00:06:39.691 --> 00:06:41.411
So after I've eliminated all the stuff

00:06:41.411 --> 00:06:42.514
that I don't need to do,

00:06:42.514 --> 00:06:44.519
the next thing I look at
before bringing on a team

00:06:44.519 --> 00:06:45.849
is actually automating.

00:06:45.849 --> 00:06:48.590
If there's anything that
I do on a consistent basis

00:06:48.590 --> 00:06:49.692
using the computer,

00:06:49.692 --> 00:06:53.249
if it's over and over and
over repetitive tasks,

00:06:53.249 --> 00:06:56.552
I immediately start to think,
how could I automate this?

00:06:56.552 --> 00:06:58.480
How can I find a software
tool to help me do this

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:01.550
or how can I hire somebody
to build a program for me

00:07:01.550 --> 00:07:02.779
to solve this problem?

00:07:02.779 --> 00:07:04.910
So as an example, using YouTube,

00:07:04.910 --> 00:07:06.259
there's a great tool called TubeBuddy

00:07:06.259 --> 00:07:09.625
that I'm the highest paying member of.

00:07:09.625 --> 00:07:13.059
I've upgraded my account
twice to pay them extra money.

00:07:13.059 --> 00:07:14.694
I'm not affiliated with them in any way

00:07:14.694 --> 00:07:16.957
but I love them because
they allow you to automate

00:07:16.957 --> 00:07:18.722
a lot of your YouTube processes.

00:07:18.722 --> 00:07:19.555
So as an example,

00:07:19.555 --> 00:07:21.787
YouTube added a new
feature called end screens

00:07:21.787 --> 00:07:24.166
where you can in the last
20 seconds of your video

00:07:24.166 --> 00:07:26.862
add some new features in
to link to other videos,

00:07:26.862 --> 00:07:28.910
subscribe to your newsletter,
subscribe to your channel,

00:07:28.910 --> 00:07:32.174
all that fun stuff but I
already had 3000 videos

00:07:32.174 --> 00:07:33.649
that didn't have these end screens

00:07:33.649 --> 00:07:36.207
and going in one by one by one by one

00:07:36.207 --> 00:07:37.550
would cause a real problem.

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:39.103
So TubeBuddy had that program

00:07:39.103 --> 00:07:40.820
and for whatever I'm paying them,

00:07:40.820 --> 00:07:44.126
$80 a month or $100 a month or
$50 a month, whatever it is,

00:07:44.126 --> 00:07:45.150
makes so much sense

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:48.460
because I can update 3000 videos at a time

00:07:48.460 --> 00:07:52.879
and so always look to
eliminate first, automate next

00:07:52.879 --> 00:07:56.962
before you move on to
bringing somebody on board.

00:07:58.820 --> 00:08:00.780
And number seven is do work that you love.

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:02.455
You are way more productive.

00:08:02.455 --> 00:08:03.724
You are way more creative.

00:08:03.724 --> 00:08:05.468
You create much better output

00:08:05.468 --> 00:08:07.063
when you're doing work that you love,

00:08:07.063 --> 00:08:09.236
if you are doing the
work that you look down

00:08:09.236 --> 00:08:10.069
and it's eight in the morning,

00:08:10.069 --> 00:08:12.258
you look up and it's suddenly
one o'clock in the afternoon,

00:08:12.258 --> 00:08:13.412
you look back down, you look back up,

00:08:13.412 --> 00:08:14.718
it's six o'clock at night.

00:08:14.718 --> 00:08:16.802
When you're doing work that you love,

00:08:16.802 --> 00:08:19.098
you're going to have a much better output

00:08:19.098 --> 00:08:20.737
than when you're doing work that you hate.

00:08:20.737 --> 00:08:22.583
You know that work that you hate.

00:08:22.583 --> 00:08:23.731
You struggle through it.

00:08:23.731 --> 00:08:25.544
You try to find ways to avoid it.

00:08:25.544 --> 00:08:27.879
You force yourself to do it but
it's not going to be very good

00:08:27.879 --> 00:08:31.643
and it takes way, way, way
longer than somebody who loves it

00:08:31.643 --> 00:08:33.642
and it's not just about skill.

00:08:33.642 --> 00:08:35.605
Somebody who loves it
might be better skill,

00:08:35.605 --> 00:08:37.035
they can get it done faster

00:08:37.035 --> 00:08:38.722
but if you had equal skill level,

00:08:38.722 --> 00:08:40.118
they'll still get it done faster

00:08:40.118 --> 00:08:41.630
because they love the process.

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:43.962
When you love it, you want
to spend time doing it

00:08:43.962 --> 00:08:47.275
and it goes much quicker
than if you don't love it

00:08:47.275 --> 00:08:49.000
and it feels like a chore.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:49.980
So those are the seven ways

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:52.679
that smart people work
less and get more done.

00:08:52.679 --> 00:08:55.871
I'd love to know which one
did you guys like the most.

00:08:55.871 --> 00:08:58.006
What are you going to immediately
apply maybe to your life

00:08:58.006 --> 00:08:59.927
or your business after
watching this video?

00:08:59.927 --> 00:09:01.478
Did I miss an eight, nine, 10

00:09:01.478 --> 00:09:03.149
that you want to add in as well?

00:09:03.149 --> 00:09:04.456
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:09:04.456 --> 00:09:06.091
I'm really curious to find out.

